+# Changes
+
+## Round 1
+
+Addressed the two failing groups in REVIEW.md's held-out suite report.
+
+- Group "undefined" (4 failures): a key whose value is `undefined` now counts as not given. In `src/layer.mjs`, `merge` skips `undefined` values in `over` (so `base`'s value, or its object, is kept and a key only `over` has with `undefined` does not appear, at any depth), and `copy` leaves out `undefined` values so none reach the result. I applied the same rule to `base` for consistency, so the result never holds an `undefined` value (a judgement call; the report only specified `over`). `undefined` inside arrays is unchanged, since positions matter.
+- Group "not plain data" (7 failures): added `assertPlainData` in `src/layer.mjs`, run on both arguments before merging. A function, Map, Set or class instance anywhere (nested objects, inside arrays, in `base` or `over`, even a `base` value that `over` would replace) throws a `TypeError`. Values under forbidden keys are not checked since they are dropped. `Date` values are still accepted and copied, as before (the checklist treats `Date` as data in values; it is only refused as an argument).
+- Note on checklist item 4 (shared references for such values): resolved by the same change, since those values are now refused rather than copied by reference.
+- Tests added in `tests/layer.test.mjs`: undefined-in-over (all four reported cases plus nested), undefined-in-base, refusal of function/Map/Set/class instance in many positions, and Dates/null still accepted.
+- Round 0 items 1-8 were reported satisfied; their behaviour is unchanged.
+- `CHANGELOG.md` line left as is.
